(Bug #71 reaches the expression form of a hole too - `{ratio multiply 2.0:x}`
 printed the product's IEEE-754 bits. An expression hole has no name of its
 own to quote back, so the caret anchors on the first name inside it and the
 help names the way out that works: a cast cannot be written inside the hole,
 because the braces a whole-expression cast needs (LANGUAGE.md:1860) are the
 hole's own.)

a float called ratio is 2.5.
Print "{ratio multiply 2.0:x}".
